.TH snip-query 1 "" "snip 0.6.3" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-query \- query and inspect snippets without modifying them
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip list\fR [\fB\-\-folder\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-subfolders\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip search\fR [\fB\-\-regex\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-subfolders\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-field\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-context\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIQUERY\fR> 
\fBsnip show\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip cat\fR [\fB\-\-fragment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip preview\fR [\fB\-\-render\fR] [\fB\-\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip path\fR [\fB\-\-metadata\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\fR] [\fB\-\-fragment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip open\fR [\fB\-\-metadata\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\fR] [\fB\-\-fragment\fR] [\fB\-\-app\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip info\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Read and inspect snippets without modifying them. list returns summaries, search returns scored matching lines, show returns one complete snippet, cat prints raw fragment bytes, preview renders human\-facing output, path resolves managed files, open launches an application, and info reports library counts.
.PP
A snippet selector is resolved as a package path relative to snippets, a UUID prefix of at least eight hexadecimal digits, or an exact case\-sensitive title. Ambiguous titles are conflicts. Fragment selectors are a 1\-based index or a fragment UUID prefix.
.PP
For list and search, \-\-folder includes the named folder and all descendants. Add \-\-no\-subfolders for only the direct folder, and pass \-\-folder "" for Uncategorized. Folder matching is case\-insensitive on complete path components. \-\-tag restricts results to one tag.
.PP
Use show for structured content and fingerprints, cat for pipelines, and preview for people. JSON and JSONL output contracts are documented in snip\-agents(7).
.PP
When cat is used without \-\-fragment on a snippet containing multiple fragments, it still prints only fragment 1 and writes a selection note to standard error.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip list"
List snippets without their full content
.TP
\fB\-\-folder\fR \fI<FOLDER>\fR
Restrict to a folder and its subfolders. Pass "" for Uncategorized
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-subfolders\fR
Restrict \-\-folder to that folder alone, excluding its subfolders
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Restrict results to snippets carrying this tag
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR [default: modified]
Order of the listing. Pinned snippets always come first
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
modified: Most recently modified first. Legacy `manual` config values migrate here
.IP \(bu 2
title: Case\-insensitive title, ascending
.IP \(bu 2
created: Most recently created first
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS "snip search"
Search titles, tags, notes, and fragment content
.TP
\fB\-\-regex\fR
Treat QUERY as a regular expression. Case\-insensitive; use (?\-i) to opt out
.TP
\fB\-\-folder\fR \fI<FOLDER>\fR
Restrict to a folder and its subfolders. Pass "" for Uncategorized
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-subfolders\fR
Restrict \-\-folder to that folder alone, excluding its subfolders
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Restrict results to snippets carrying this tag
.TP
\fB\-\-field\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Only search these parts of a snippet. Repeatable; defaults to all
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
title
.IP \(bu 2
tag
.IP \(bu 2
readme
.IP \(bu 2
content
.IP \(bu 2
note
.RE
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-context\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 0]
Lines of surrounding context to include with each match
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Keep only the top N results after scoring
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIQUERY\fR>
Text or regular expression to find
.SS "snip show"
Show a complete snippet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip cat"
Print one fragment with no decorations
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\fR \fI<FRAGMENT>\fR
1\-based index or fragment UUID prefix
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip preview"
Render a snippet for terminal or HTML preview
.TP
\fB\-\-render\fR \fI<RENDER>\fR
Rendering format. Defaults to the configured preview format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
ansi
.IP \(bu 2
plain
.IP \(bu 2
html
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pager\fR
Send output through the configured pager or $PAGER
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable a pager enabled in the config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip path"
Print a managed filesystem path
.TP
\fB\-\-metadata\fR
Print the path to snippet.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\fR
Print the path to README.md
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\fR \fI<FRAGMENT>\fR
Print the path to a fragment selected by 1\-based index or UUID prefix
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip open"
Open a managed path in an external application
.TP
\fB\-\-metadata\fR
Open snippet.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\fR
Open README.md
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\fR \fI<FRAGMENT>\fR
Open a fragment selected by 1\-based index or UUID prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<APP>\fR
Command to launch. Defaults to the `gui_editor` config key, then `code`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip info"
Show library metadata and counts
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "EXAMPLES"
List every snippet below the Code folder carrying the rust tag:
.RS 4
.nf
snip list \-\-folder Code \-\-tag rust
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search content and notes with two lines of context, keeping ten matches:
.RS 4
.nf
snip \-\-output json search deploy \-\-field content \-\-field note \-\-context 2 \-\-limit 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print the second fragment exactly as stored:
.RS 4
.nf
snip cat 79d92dea \-\-fragment 2
.fi
.RE
